diff --git a/board/qualcomm/CAPRI-UPSTREAM-PORT.md b/board/qualcomm/CAPRI-UPSTREAM-PORT.md
new file mode 100644
index 00000000..b2c3e735
--- /dev/null
+++ b/board/qualcomm/CAPRI-UPSTREAM-PORT.md
@@ -0,0 +1,84 @@
+# Motorola Moto G10 Power XT2127-4: upstream U-Boot port
+
+Base: official upstream U-Boot `v2026.07` (`ece349ad`).
+Branch: `capri-safe-handoff`.
+
+## Why the device-tree-only experiment failed
+
+The previous `capri-dt-only` build was accepted by Motorola ABL through
+`fastboot boot`, but stayed at the Motorola splash screen with no menu.
+The actual failure point was not observable without an early debug console.
+The default Qualcomm environment initially didn't automatically show a menu;
+fixing that alone did not resolve the failure.
+
+The compiled C `save_boot_params()` in the earlier build performed a stack
+push before ARM64 stack setup. The replacement assembly captures ABL's
+incoming `x0` without touching the stack. The custom Capri memory path is
+necessary for our currently verified design: the internal DT describes U-Boot
+drivers, whereas the *live* ABL DT describes RAM and firmware reservations.
+The stock Android device-tree files have a zero-sized `/memory` placeholder,
+so copying static memory values is unsafe. The port validates and imports
+runtime RAM, reserves firmware carveouts and framebuffer memory, selects a
+safe relocation arena, and protects no-map areas and EFI memory descriptors.
+
+This branch deliberately reuses the exact handoff and memory-protection code
+that previously booted successfully on the handset, on top of **official**
+U-Boot. The Tauchgang Samsung patches, CI and branding have not been ported.
+The three relevant differences in upstream Linux DT includes are overridden
+in the Capri board DTS to reproduce the previously tested tree's properties.
+
+This is a *smallest known-working-behavior port*, not a claim that all custom
+Capri code is theoretically unavoidable. Simplify it **after** hardware
+verification, one change at a time.
+
+## Reproducible build and package
+
+From this checkout on the ARM64 NixOS build host:
+
+```sh
+nix-shell ../capri-build-tools/shell-uboot.nix --run \
+  'python3 ../capri-build-tools/build-uboot.py . ../capri-upstream-safe-output --jobs 8'
+```
+
+The builder currently retains a historical `Tauchgang U-Boot` *string in its
+JSON metadata* because it is shared with the earlier project. The binary
+built from this branch is official U-Boot with our Capri patches, not Tauchgang.
+
+Expected image: `../capri-upstream-safe-output/boot-uboot-capri-v3.img`.
+Its Android v3 header uses an ARM64 `0x80000` text offset and a 50-byte
+empty ramdisk, compatible with the previously tested packaging layout.
+
+## Host validation already completed
+
+- Clean compilation against official upstream `v2026.07`.
+- U-Boot's `binary_size_check` and `init_sp_bss_offset_check` completed.
+- Initial historical builds had write functions disabled by configuration;
+  the separate Nix patch now enables MMC, FAT, ext4 and GPT write support.
+- The resulting `.config` was byte-identical to the previous hardware-tested
+  Tauchgang build's `.config`.
+- Early ARM64 `save_boot_params` object disassembly contains only PC-relative
+  pointer calculation, store of `x0`, and branch; no stack instructions.
+- Compiled control DT is 59,920 bytes, with only display `resets` property
+  ordering differing from the previously tested control DT; semantic values
+  match.
+- `unpack_bootimg` verified version 3, header and payload sizes; extracted
+  kernel and ramdisk are byte-identical to packaged inputs.
+- `git diff --check` passes.
+
+These are **host-only** tests. No boot on hardware of this *upstream* binary has
+been observed yet. Do not claim it works until the menu and shell appear.
+
+## First device test (temporary only)
+
+With a known-good fallback available and the XT2127-4 in ABL fastboot mode,
+copy the image to the USB-attached `ideapad` host and use:
+
+```sh
+fastboot boot /tmp/boot-uboot-capri-upstream-safe-v3.img
+```
+
+**Do not use `fastboot flash`, erase, or modify `vendor_boot`/`dtbo`.**
+Confirm that the menu is visible, volume/power keys respond, USB ACM console
+appears after enabling it, `mmc info` and `part list mmc 0` succeed, and
+`bootefi hello` returns. If the splash screen remains, collect video or USB
+observations to distinguish early relocation, display and input failures.
diff --git a/board/qualcomm/CAPRI-UPSTREAM-SIMPLIFICATION-AUDIT.md b/board/qualcomm/CAPRI-UPSTREAM-SIMPLIFICATION-AUDIT.md
new file mode 100644
index 00000000..5e1916b2
--- /dev/null
+++ b/board/qualcomm/CAPRI-UPSTREAM-SIMPLIFICATION-AUDIT.md
@@ -0,0 +1,125 @@
+# Capri U-Boot: audit of generic upstream RAM/handoff support
+
+Base: **official U-Boot v2026.07**, Capri verified on handset using branch
+`capri-safe-handoff` commit `f726c188`. This audit is source inspection,
+**not** an additional device boot test. Baseline is not modified.
+
+## What works upstream already
+
+- `arch/arm/mach-snapdragon/board.c:board_fdt_blob_setup()` obtains the ABL
+  FDT from `get_prev_bl_fdt_addr()` and can parse its `/memory` if the internal
+  DT has none. The result populates U-Boot's RAM-bank list.
+- `boot/image-fdt.c:boot_fdt_add_mem_rsv_regions()` knows FDT reserve-map
+  entries and `/reserved-memory` with `no-map`; `lib/lmb.c:lmb_reserve_common()`
+  invokes it on the **selected control DT**.
+- `common/memtop.c:get_mem_top()` finds a gap that avoids reservations in a
+  **single contiguous RAM region** supplied by the caller.
+- `lib/efi_loader/efi_dt_fixup.c:efi_carve_out_dt_rsv()` handles reserved
+  regions in the **payload DT** when the EFI DT-fixup protocol is used.
+- `lib/efi_loader/efi_memory.c:efi_add_known_memory()` is a weak extension
+  point for reserving additional firmware/board regions.
+- Generic Qualcomm simple-framebuffer, eMMC and input paths work on the
+  confirmed Capri build with minimal DT and driver quirks.
+
+## Missing integration: why copying only the DTS was insufficient
+
+1. `arch/arm/cpu/armv8/start.S` calls `save_boot_params` **before the normal
+   stack is initialized**. Upstream C implementation in
+   `arch/arm/lib/save_prev_bl_data.c` compiled to `stp x29, x30, [sp, #-16]!`
+   on our build host. The working stack-free assembly (`save_boot_params.S`)
+   captures incoming x0 safely, without relying on incoming SP. This is a
+   generic ARM64 defect for the enabled previous-bootloader save path, not
+   Capri-specific hardware logic; it merits an upstreamable generic patch.
+2. `board_fdt_blob_setup()` chooses the **internal device tree** for U-Boot
+   driver bindings and only borrows **RAM bank geometry** from ABL's device
+   tree. It does not merge ABL's *reserved-memory* and FDT memreserve map.
+   Therefore LMB cannot see them from the control DT, despite supporting
+   reservations itself. The Android stock DT uses `/memory` placeholders,
+   so hard-coding the bank layout would also be wrong.
+3. `board_get_usable_ram_top()` defaults to RAM top and does not check
+   firmware carveouts at **pre-relocation** time. `get_mem_top()` accounts
+   for reservations but accepts only a single `[base, size)` pair. Our ABL
+   geometry can contain multiple banks and gaps; using one span directly
+   would allow relocation into an unavailable hole. The Capri hook explicitly
+   scans each bank and requires space for the *entire* pre-relocation arena,
+   not only `gd->mon_len`.
+4. `arch/arm/mach-snapdragon/board.c:carve_out_reserved_memory()` runs only
+   for **qcom,qcs404**, and runs after page table setup. Capri's existing
+   patch instead builds page tables with `no-map` holes already absent while
+   explicitly permitting the inherited framebuffer. Simply importing DT
+   nodes is not enough to make the ARM64 MMU map safe.
+5. `efi_carve_out_dt_rsv()` reserves ranges from the **EFI payload's DT**;
+   when a different payload DT is submitted, those may not include ABL
+   reservations. The Capri hook restores authoritative control-tree firmware
+   reservations with `efi_add_known_memory()`. This protects the EFI map.
+6. The static Capri DT is for mainline U-Boot drivers, not downstream ABL
+   phandles. Replacing it wholesale with the ABL DT can break eMMC, display,
+   USB and buttons; different bindings must not be blindly merged.
+
+## Functions in `capri.c` and reduction opportunities
+
+| Current function | Can existing generic upstream code replace it unchanged? | Conclusion |
+|---|---|---|
+| `qcom_capri_merge_fdt`, `import_memory` | No | Generic Qualcomm hook should merge *runtime* bank geometry with validation; do not import all downstream hardware nodes. |
+| `import_reservations`, `reserve_range` | Not without glue | Generic libfdt + LMB can consume a merged control DT; need pre-relocation, multi-bank, overlap-checked import. |
+| `board_get_usable_ram_top` | No | Generalize `get_mem_top` to multiple banks + full arena size, or keep a small Qualcomm wrapper. |
+| `qcom_capri_mem_map` | No | Build `no-map` holes into both MMU page tables; existing QCS404 carveout path doesn't cover Capri. |
+| `efi_add_known_memory` | Partly | Generic EFI extension hook exists; must keep an authoritative source for firmware reservations independent of the payload DT. |
+| FDT board-ID, bounds, alignment checks | Should remain | This is safety-critical validation of untrusted runtime firmware input. |
+| Fixed framebuffer reservation/exemption | Board specific | Must be specified explicitly, ideally from a DT reserved-memory + simple-framebuffer relationship rather than raw address literals. |
+
+## Upstreamable patch strategy (one independently testable step each)
+
+1. **ARM64 previous-BL x0 capture:** isolate the stack-free saver in generic
+   `arch/arm/lib`; build/test the assembly with `sp=0` and preserve x0.
+2. **Qualcomm DT handoff:** introduce an opt-in generic firmware-memory merge
+   before DRAM/relocation, retaining the mainline control DT for devices.
+   Unit test multiple bank ranges, overlapping and unaligned reservations,
+   DT buffer bounds, and FDT reserve map.
+3. **Relocation selection:** introduce a generic multi-bank reserved-region
+   placement helper, including complete U-Boot relocation arena footprint.
+   Test RAM holes and rejected invalid layouts.
+4. **MMU no-map:** preconstruct both page tables without mapped secure
+   firmware regions, using an opt-in generic Qualcomm path; verify the
+   framebuffer exception and number of descriptors.
+5. **EFI reservations:** ensure the board/firmware reserved ranges cannot be
+   downgraded when a different EFI payload FDT is supplied.
+6. Replace `CONFIG_MOTOROLA_CAPRI`-specific branching with generic opt-in
+   Kconfig once stepwise builds and actual device tests pass.
+
+**Do not remove the existing code wholesale.** Existing upstream mechanisms
+handle only parts of this pipeline; the verified 531-line `capri.c` currently
+connects them at several *different boot stages*. The failed DTS-only image
+cannot isolate which missing stage caused the hang. No new simplified image
+should be called verified until boot menu, USB serial, eMMC and EFI smoke
+checks pass on the actual XT2127-4.
+
+## Device-tree comparison on actual XT2127-4 (2026-11-12)
+
+Temporary boot of verified upstream-safe image. USB ACM shell enabled at the
+on-screen menu. All FDT commands were read-only; no partition was flashed.
+
+- ABL-passed tree: `prevbl_fdt_addr=454c4000`; `/memory` contains three
+  populated bank pairs: `(0x40000000,0x3dd00000)`,
+  `(0xc0000000,0x80000000)`, `(0x80000000,0x40000000)`.
+  Original Motorola `hyp_region@45700000` and
+  `cont_splash_region@5c000000` reservations present.
+- Original appended U-Boot DTB: `0x401e5890` = load base `0x40080000`
+  + nodtb image length `0x165890`. Its `/memory@80000000` is **still
+  zero-sized**, and its reserved-memory entries retain the upstream DTS
+  naming. ABL did **not** fix up the appended DTB on this test.
+- Active U-Boot control DTB: `fdtcontroladdr=13f587c70`, also reported by
+  `bdinfo` as `fdt_blob`. It uses the mainline compatible
+  `motorola,capri`, `qcom,sm4250`, has the three populated, sorted RAM
+  banks, and contains imported `firmware-0@45700000` with `no-map`.
+  `bdinfo` confirms active framebuffer `0x5c000000` and LMB firmware
+  reservations; relocated U-Boot starts at `0x13fdb5000`.
+- U-Boot's `fdt addr -c` **only prints** the control-FDT address, it does
+  not change the working FDT used by `fdt print`. We explicitly selected
+  each address with `fdt addr ADDRESS` before printing properties.
+
+**Result:** For this Motorola ABL implementation, upstream U-Boot cannot
+rely on ABL populating the appended mainline DTB. The safe port's merge
+of the separate runtime vendor DTB into a mainline control DTB is necessary
+for its current memory-management approach. Genericizing that merge is
+reasonable; dropping it without replacing its protection is not.
diff --git a/board/qualcomm/QCOM-ABL-MEMORY-HANDOFF.md b/board/qualcomm/QCOM-ABL-MEMORY-HANDOFF.md
new file mode 100644
index 00000000..7ee55e89
--- /dev/null
+++ b/board/qualcomm/QCOM-ABL-MEMORY-HANDOFF.md
@@ -0,0 +1,107 @@
+# Qualcomm ABL memory handoff (Moto G10 Power hardware-verified)
+
+## Why this exists
+
+On the Motorola Moto G10 Power XT2127-4 (Capri, Qualcomm SM4250), ABL
+passes a *separate* vendor FDT in x0. The appended mainline U-Boot DTB is
+not fixed up with live RAM geometry. Replacing the mainline DT with the
+vendor DT would also lose the upstream driver bindings.
+
+`CONFIG_QCOM_ABL_MEMORY_HANDOFF` opts into an early merge implemented by
+`arch/arm/mach-snapdragon/qcom-abl-memory.c`. The mainline DT remains the
+control tree; the module imports only runtime memory banks and protected
+firmware reservations. The stack-free ARM64 x0 saver is still necessary.
+
+## Board-defined properties
+
+The Capri control DT in
+`dts/upstream/src/arm64/qcom/sm4250-motorola-capri-power.dts` supplies:
+
+- `qcom,board-id = <0x500 0xb200>`: must match the firmware root property.
+- `u-boot,abl-compatible = "qcom,bengal-capri"`: required matching
+  compatible in the firmware root node.
+- An enabled `simple-framebuffer` child of `/chosen` with `reg =
+  <0 0x5c000000 0 0x465000>` and `#address-cells = <2>`,
+  `#size-cells = <2>` on `/chosen`.
+
+The framebuffer parser uses the parent's cell counts, checks tuple length,
+page alignment, nonzero size, overflow, and requires exactly one enabled
+simple-framebuffer. A missing or malformed framebuffer fails the merge;
+no unsafe "unreserved framebuffer" fallback is permitted. The parsed
+range is used for both the reserve map and the existing MMU exception.
+
+**Do not confuse the configured 0x465000-byte simple-framebuffer range with
+ABL's larger 0x1000000-byte firmware splash reservation.** The latter is
+also imported and remains protected.
+
+## Preserved safety-critical mechanisms
+
+- Bound-checked FDT validation and runtime RAM-bank import.
+- Firmware `/reserved-memory` and FDT reserve-map import, including
+  no-map semantics; no vendor hardware phandles are imported.
+- Multi-bank, reservation-aware pre-relocation arena selection.
+- Pre-MMU page-table construction with firmware no-map holes, retaining
+  the inherited framebuffer mapping.
+- EFI reservation of authoritative control-DT firmware ranges.
+
+The relocation, MMU hole construction, and EFI algorithms have **not**
+been redesigned. Generalizing these remains higher risk and is out of
+scope for the currently hardware-verified port.
+
+## Hardware verification: 2026-11-12
+
+Tested on the real XT2127-4 using **temporary `fastboot boot` only**. No
+flash, erase, or partition mutation was performed.
+
+| Commit | Change | Hardware evidence |
+| --- | --- | --- |
+| `82ce1375` | Restored proven Capri firmware-ID and framebuffer policy in generic module | U-Boot menu, USB ACM, RAM, eMMC, GPT, `bootefi hello` |
+| `b0d4289e` | Expected `qcom,board-id` sourced from control DT | USB ACM, matching live board IDs, unchanged RAM, `bootefi hello` |
+| `c5164383` | Required vendor compatible sourced from control DT | U-Boot menu confirmed; no serial/EFI test recorded at that commit |
+| `bedcdf2c` | Framebuffer address and size sourced from simple-framebuffer DT | USB ACM, active framebuffer, memory reservations, eMMC, `bootefi hello` |
+
+Last hardware-verified commit: **`bedcdf2c`** on
+`qcom-abl-dt-framebuffer`. The active U-Boot console reported
+`U-Boot 2026.07-00010-gbedcdf2c5592`.
+
+Observed memory geometry: `(0x40000000, 0x3dd00000)`,
+`(0x80000000, 0x40000000)`, `(0xc0000000, 0x80000000)`.
+The relocation address was `0x13fdb5000`; the ABL firmware FDT was
+`0x454c4000`; video was `720x1600x32` at `0x5c000000`.
+U-Boot's LMB dump listed 13 reserved regions; the firmware's
+`0x5c000000..0x5cffffff` splash area remained reserved. The control
+FDT pointer can differ slightly with binary layout, and is not fixed.
+
+Read-only smoke-test commands in the U-Boot USB serial shell:
+
+```text
+version
+bdinfo
+printenv prevbl_fdt_addr fdtcontroladdr
+fdt addr ${fdtcontroladdr}
+fdt print /chosen/framebuffer@5c000000
+mmc list
+mmc dev 0
+mmc info
+bootefi hello
+```
+
+For every future behavioral change, build an independent v3 boot image,
+run `fastboot boot <image>` (never `fastboot flash`), verify the on-screen
+menu, enable USB ACM, inspect `bdinfo`/reservations/framebuffer, check
+read-only eMMC discovery and `bootefi hello`, then reboot to Android.
+Keep a separate known-good image and Git commit available for recovery.
+
+## Remaining work
+
+Low-risk work: documentation, comments, board-specific configuration and
+focused negative-case tests for invalid FDT inputs. No genericity claim has
+been proven on a second Qualcomm handset; only Capri is hardware tested.
+Higher-risk redesigns (relocation, ARM64 argument capture, MMU, EFI, and
+scratch-buffer policy) should remain unchanged unless addressed and tested
+independently.
+
+The earlier simplification audit at
+`board/qualcomm/CAPRI-UPSTREAM-SIMPLIFICATION-AUDIT.md` is historical:
+its references to `capri.c` and proposed hard-coded framebuffer cleanup
+reflect the state before these subsequent changes.
